---
// Written for the IT Act 2000, SPDI Rules 2011 and the DPDP Act 2023 / DPDP Rules 2025.
// Have a lawyer in India review before publishing. Never claim certification or "full compliance".
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import { site, legal, known, analyticsEnabled } from '../content/site';
import { pages } from '../content/pages';

const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ['who', '1. Who we are'],
  ['collect', '2. What we collect'],
  ['why', '3. Why we use it'],
  ['consent', '4. Consent and withdrawal'],
  ['share', '5. Who we share it with'],
  ['where', '6. Where it is stored'],
  ['keep', '7. How long we keep it'],
  ['rights', '8. Your rights'],
  ['children', '9. Children'],
  ['cookies', '10. Cookies and analytics'],
  ['security', '11. Security and breaches'],
  ['grievance', '12. Grievance Officer'],
  ['changes', '13. Changes to this policy'],
];
const mail = `mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`;
const r = legal.retention;
---
<Legal
  page={pages.privacy}
  name="Privacy Policy"
  sections={sections}
  summary={[
    'We collect only what you send us (the contact form, WhatsApp, email or phone) and, for interns, the details needed to run the program and issue certificates.',
    'We use it to reply, prepare quotes, deliver projects, run the internship and let people check certificates. We do not sell it.',
    'A few named providers handle it for us, such as our host and our email service. Some store data outside India.',
    'This site sets one cookie, only when an intern signs in to the dashboard, and shows no advertising.',
    `You can ask to see, correct or delete your data, or withdraw consent, by writing to ${site.privacyEmail}.`,
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>This website, {site.url.replace('https://', '')}, is run by {site.legalName} ("{site.name}", "we", "us"), {site.address.display}. Email <a href={mail}>{site.privacyEmail}</a>, phone <a href={`tel:${site.phone.e164}`}>{site.phone.display}</a>.</p>
  <p>For personal data collected through this site, we are the data fiduciary: we decide why and how it is used.</p>

  <h2 id="collect">2. What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you send an enquiry</h3>
  <p>The contact form asks for your name, a phone number or email address, your business name (optional), what you need, a budget range (optional) and your message. We also record that you ticked the consent box.</p>
  <h3>When you message, email or call us</h3>
  <p>Whatever you choose to send on WhatsApp or by email, and your number or address so we can reply.</p>
  <h3>If you are an intern</h3>
  <p>Your name, email, phone number, college, course, internship domain, batch, mentor, start and end dates, progress, attendance and tasks completed, the profile links you give us (GitHub, LinkedIn, portfolio), your photo if you provide one, mentor remarks, and your certificate number and certificate file.</p>
  <h3>When someone checks a certificate</h3>
  <p>The certificate check shows anyone who enters a valid Internship ID the intern's name, Internship ID, certificate number, domain, batch, start and end dates and status. It does not show contact details, college or remarks. We do not record who runs a check, apart from the technical data below.</p>
  <h3>Technical data</h3>
  <p>Our host records technical data for every request: IP address, browser and device type, the page requested and the time. We use it to keep the site running and secure.</p>

  <h2 id="why">3. Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Replying to your enquiry.</li>
    <li>Preparing a quote and, if you go ahead, delivering your project.</li>
    <li>Running the internship program and issuing certificates.</li>
    <li>Letting employers and others confirm that a certificate is genuine.</li>
    <li>Keeping the site secure and stopping spam and abuse of our forms.</li>
    {analyticsEnabled && <li>Counting page visits in aggregate to see which pages are useful.</li>}
    <li>Meeting legal obligations, such as tax records for paid work.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your data for advertising, and we do not send newsletters.</p>

  <h2 id="consent">4. Consent and withdrawal</h2>
  <p>You give consent for your enquiry by ticking the box on the contact form before sending it. Interns give consent when they join the program. When you message, email or call us yourself, we use your details only to reply.</p>
  <p>You can withdraw consent at any time by emailing <a href={mail}>{site.privacyEmail}</a> or sending "withdraw consent" on WhatsApp. That is as easy as giving it. We then stop using your data for that purpose and delete it, unless the law requires us to keep it. Withdrawal does not affect anything we did before it. For interns, withdrawing consent means we can no longer keep your certificate verifiable.</p>

  <h2 id="share">5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or rent personal data. These providers process data for us, only to provide their service:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">What it receives</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Vercel Inc.</td><td>Hosts this website and runs the contact form and certificate check</td><td>Technical data for every visit; form submissions as they pass through</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Delivers contact form submissions to our inbox</td><td>Everything you enter in the contact form</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Google (Gmail)</td><td>Our email inbox</td><td>Contact form submissions and emails you send us</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Database and file storage for intern records and certificates</td><td>Intern data listed in section 2</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Meta (WhatsApp)</td><td>Messages, if you choose to contact us on WhatsApp</td><td>Your number and the messages you send</td></tr>
      <tr><td>jsDelivr and Google Fonts</td><td>Deliver code and fonts to the intern dashboard and admin pages only</td><td>Technical data (IP address, browser) when those pages load</td></tr>
      {analyticsEnabled && <tr><td>Vercel Web Analytics</td><td>Counts page visits without cookies</td><td>Page, referrer, country and device type, not linked to you</td></tr>}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>We also share data when the law requires it, for example on a valid order from a court or government authority.</p>

  <h2 id="where">6. Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>Our providers run servers in several countries, and some of them store or process data outside India, including in the United States and the European Union. Each one is bound by its own security and privacy terms. We will follow any restriction the Government of India places on transfers to particular countries.</p>

  <h2 id="keep">7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep personal data only for as long as its purpose needs, then delete it, unless the law requires us to keep it longer.</p>
  <ul>
    {known(r.enquiries) && <li>Enquiries that do not become projects: <Fact v={r.enquiries} /></li>}
    {known(r.interns) && <li>Intern records: <Fact v={r.interns} /></li>}
    {known(r.certificates) && <li>Certificate details for the public check: <Fact v={r.certificates} /></li>}
    {known(r.logs) && <li>Hosting logs: <Fact v={r.logs} /></li>}
    <li>Project and payment records: as long as Indian tax and accounting law requires.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rights">8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you and how we use it, and who we have shared it with</li>
    <li>correct data that is wrong, complete data that is incomplete, or update it</li>
    <li>erase your data once it is no longer needed, unless the law requires us to keep it</li>
    <li>stop using your data by withdrawing consent (section 4)</li>
    <li>hear and resolve a complaint (section 12)</li>
    <li>let another person you nominate use these rights for you if you die or become unable to</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Email <a href={mail}>{site.privacyEmail}</a> from the address or number we know you by, so we can confirm it is you. We reply within one month.</p>

  <h2 id="children">9. Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not aimed at children. If an internship applicant is under 18, we process their data only after verifiable consent from a parent or legal guardian, and we do not track or profile them.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">10. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>This site sets one cookie, and only when an intern signs in to the dashboard: a strictly necessary session cookie that holds your Internship ID in signed form, so the dashboard can show your record and no one else's. It cannot be read by scripts on the page, is sent only to this site, is not used for tracking and expires after 2 hours.</p>
  {analyticsEnabled
    ? <p>We use Vercel Web Analytics, which counts visits without cookies and without identifying you. Because nothing non-essential is stored on your device, there is no cookie banner.</p>
    : <p>We do not use analytics or tracking tools.</p>}

  <h2 id="security">11. Security and breaches</h2>
  <p>Every page and form is served over HTTPS. The contact form and certificate check run on our server, which checks every input and limits repeated submissions to block spam and guessing.</p>
  <p>No system is perfectly secure. If a personal data breach happens, we will inform the people affected and the Data Protection Board of India, in the way and within the time the law requires.</p>

  <h2 id="grievance">12. Grievance Officer</h2>
  <p>
    {known(legal.grievanceOfficer) && <>Grievance Officer: <Fact v={legal.grievanceOfficer} /><br /></>}
    Email: <a href={mail}>{site.privacyEmail}</a><br />
    Address: {site.legalName}, {site.address.display}
  </p>
  <p>We acknowledge every grievance and resolve it within one month. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Data Protection Board of India.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>When we change this policy, we update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. If a change affects how we use data you already gave us, we will tell you by email or WhatsApp before it applies.</p>
</Legal>
